### Review Findings

_Code review conducted 2026-04-14 — 3 layers: Blind Hunter, Edge Case Hunter, Acceptance Auditor (fresh review)_

#### Decision Needed

- [ ] [Review][Decision] DateTime timezone inconsistency — migration uses `sa.DateTime()` (timezone-naive) for `started_at`, `timestamp`, `loaded_at`, but `Session.started_at` default produces a tz-aware datetime via `datetime.now(timezone.utc)`. asyncpg raises `DataError` at runtime when inserting a tz-aware Python datetime into a tz-naive PostgreSQL TIMESTAMP column. Fix requires `sa.DateTime(timezone=True)` in all three migration columns plus `DateTime(timezone=True)` on the ORM `mapped_column()` calls [alembic/versions/0001_initial_schema.py:27,39,71; app/models/session.py:14; app/models/interaction_log.py:19; app/models/workflow_config.py:15]
- [ ] [Review][Decision] Settings field names renamed from spec — spec mandates `DATABASE_POOL_MIN` and `DATABASE_POOL_MAX`; implementation uses `DATABASE_POOL_BASE` and `DATABASE_POOL_OVERFLOW` consistently across config.py, engine.py, docker-compose.yml, and conftest.py. Accept the rename (story spec should be updated) or revert to spec names?

#### Patches

- [ ] [Review][Patch] `InteractionLog.timestamp` has no default — `nullable=False` column with no `default` or `server_default`; any insert omitting `timestamp` raises IntegrityError [app/models/interaction_log.py:19]
- [ ] [Review][Patch] `WorkflowConfig.loaded_at` has no default — same pattern; `nullable=False` with no `default` or `server_default` [app/models/workflow_config.py:15]
- [ ] [Review][Patch] `pytest.ini` missing `asyncio_default_fixture_loop_scope = session` — session-scoped `async def engine()` fixture with `asyncio_mode = auto` requires this in pytest-asyncio 0.21+; without it, event loop may tear down before fixture teardown completes [autom9-backend/pytest.ini]
- [ ] [Review][Patch] `test_missing_env_var_exits` tests pydantic `ValidationError`, not `sys.exit(1)` — test instantiates a local `PartialSettings` class and never exercises `app.core.config`; AC4 requires verifying the app exits with a clear error message on missing vars [tests/test_health.py:24]
- [ ] [Review][Patch] `uv.lock*` glob in Dockerfile COPY — shell glob means absent lockfile silently passes the COPY step; `uv sync --frozen` then fails with a confusing error; use `COPY pyproject.toml uv.lock ./` [autom9-backend/Dockerfile:9]
- [ ] [Review][Patch] `CredentialStore` `UniqueConstraint` generates misleading name — naming convention `uq_%(table_name)s_%(column_0_name)s` encodes only `org_id`, producing `uq_credential_store_org_id` which implies single-column uniqueness; constraint is functionally correct but name is misleading [alembic/versions/0001_initial_schema.py:62]
- [ ] [Review][Patch] `db_session` SAVEPOINT pattern incomplete — `begin_nested()` creates SAVEPOINT but no `after_transaction_end` event listener re-establishes it after `session.commit()` is called inside a test; write tests that commit will have degraded isolation [tests/conftest.py:35-43]

